d\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-24\nValid as Of: 2024-08-24\nVersion: 2407\n\n", "--- Record 1891 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Properties to Optimize Search Performance\nDescription: Two new properties tc.pp.user_types and tc.pp.search_operation can be set up to optimize the performance of the people search engine for very large user groups.  For more information, see Identity Directory Connectivity.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-19\nValid as Of: 2024-11-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1892 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Istio module: Deletion of the annotation disable-external-name-alias\nDescription: The annotation disable-external-name-alias is scheduled to be deleted on 04.11 in the fast channel and on 18.11 in the regular channel. See the deprecation note.Required action: If you are using the annotation, follow themigration guide and adjust your resources’ configuration to align with Istio’s behavior.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deleted\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-13\nValid as Of: 2024-11-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1893 ---\nComponent: Graph\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Business Data Graph Editor\nDescription: You can edit your business data graph directly in Graph on Integration Suite.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-18\nValid as Of: 2024-11-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1894 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Application Connector module: Documentation\nDescription: We're excited to announce that the Application Connector module documentation is now live on Help Portal. To learn more about connecting your workflows deployed on Kyma with external solutions, see Application Connector Module.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-18\nValid as Of: 2024-11-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1895 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Istio module: Update to version 1.10.0\nDescription: As announced in the deprecation note, we've removed support for the istio-operator.kyma-project.io/disable-external-name-alias annotation. From now on, setting the annotation will have no effect.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-04\nValid as Of: 2024-11-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1896 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Developer's Guide\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Automate the Provisioning of Resources Needed to Create a Kyma Cluster\nDescription: Using the Terraform provider for SAP BTP, you can now automate the provisioning of resources needed to create a Kyma cluster, deploy applications, run tests, and tear down the resources when they are no longer required.   See Terraforming Kyma Runtimes.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-18\nValid as Of: 2024-11-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1897 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Add or Remove Rows of Table Form\nDescription: By default process participants can add or remove table rows from a table form.For more information, see Form Tables.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-18\nValid as Of: 2024-11-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1898 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Deprecation of Manage Country/Region Groups App\nDescription: The Manage Country/Region Groups app has now been deprecated and will be deleted with an upcoming release. Instead, for reporting purposes, use the Manage Company Code Groups app that was released in February 2024 and allows for more detailed reporting based on company codes.  Remember  You can find more information about the new reporting approach under Reporting on Task Execution and Task Overall Level.  App affected:  Manage Country/Region Groups\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-31\nValid as Of: 2024-11-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1899 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Ready-Only Setting for Migration Apps\nDescription: The two apps Migrate Configuration Data and Migrate Closing Task Lists have now been set to read-only. The two apps were previously used to help customers migrate from the deprecated solution SAP S/4HANA Cloud for advanced financial closing that was part of SAP S/4HANA Cloud to the SAP BTP solution SAP Advanced Financial Closing.  Apps affected:  Migrate Configuration Data  Migrate Closing Task Lists  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-31\nValid as Of: 2024-11-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1900 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Built-In Support\nDescription: As of this release you can", " SAP Advanced Financial Closing.  Apps affected:  Migrate Configuration Data  Migrate Closing Task Lists  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-31\nValid as Of: 2024-11-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1900 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Built-In Support\nDescription: As of this release you can access the built-in support for SAP Advanced Financial Closing in all apps. The built-in support provides links to documentation relevant to the specific app you're in and even allows you to search for more help, such as other documentation pages.Note  The built-in support feature won't be available right away on the actual release date, but will follow shortly. No action from you is required.  You can access the built-in support by choosing the headset icon  in the header bar of any app.  Apps affected: All apps\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-31\nValid as Of: 2024-11-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 3111 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Public Workspace: Access for Non-Member External Users.\nDescription: External users who are not workspace members are unable to search for a workspace or see content uploaded by members. However, when adding a specific external user to the Access Policy user list, that user can explore and find this workspace, be invited to the workspace, be mentioned in chats, and see content uploaded by the workspace members.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-18\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3112 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Removal of External Workspace Type\nDescription:   It's no longer possible to create an external workspace. When you create a new workspace, you can choose between creating a public workspace or a private workspace.  Existing external workspaces will become private workspaces and an External warning icon will be added to the workspace header to indicate that the content of this workspace is visible to external users.  You can invite external users to both private and public workspaces. To do that, when you create a new workspace (or when you edit the admin settings of an existing workspace), you need to choose the option \"External users can access this workspace and be invited as members\". Note that the invited external users should already be added to the system prior to the invitation. For more information about external users, seeAbout External Users  If the workspace setting \"Allow users to request to join this workspace\" is enabled, users can request to join this workspace by going to Workspaces  View All Workspaces   Explore Workspaces and clicking Join Workspace next to the workspace name. Alternatively, they can open the workspace and click the Join button at the top right.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-14\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3113 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Role-Based Filtering of Cards\nDescription: With the transition to the Content Manager as the card management tool, all cards will be assigned to roles and will be accessible at runtime based on user roles.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-18\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3114 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support Custom SMTP Configuration\nDescription: Customers can choose to use their own SMTP server settings instead of the default settings. To configure the SMTP settings, go to Admin Console, External Integration  SMTP Configuration and add the custom SMTP settings. To go back to the default SMTP settings, simply delete the custom configuration.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-18\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3115 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support of Cards as App Visualization Type\nDescription:   Cards are now supported as a visualization type of local apps and are maintained in the Content Manager - App editor – Visualization tab.  It is no longer possible to manually upload standalone cards or update cards through the Admin Console. Remaining functionality in the Admin Console is configuring the card and enabling/disabling the card.   It is no longer possible to directly deploy a card created via the Development Tools for SAP Build Work Zone extension in SAP Business Application Studio to the subaccount.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-18\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3116 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support of Custom Domains in Private Networks\nDescription: To support the use of a custom domain resolvable only in customer’s own private networks, customers should open a support ticket on component EP-WZ-DMN to request this. Further instructions will be provided by the support team.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-18\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3117 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: System Info on the Overview Page\nDescription: The Overview page of a workspace has been enhanced with additional information that can be added to support tickets.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-18\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3118 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: CSRF Protection for Dynamic Destinations\nDescription: Today our approuters do not provide CSRF protection for dynamic destinations. It’s assumed that backends behind the destinations, handle CSRF protection on their own.   New security measures have been introduced to enable CSRF protection by the approuter. This is done by setting the CEP.EnableCsrfProtection property to true for all dynamic destinations where their respective backend doesn", "8 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: CSRF Protection for Dynamic Destinations\nDescription: Today our approuters do not provide CSRF protection for dynamic destinations. It’s assumed that backends behind the destinations, handle CSRF protection on their own.   New security measures have been introduced to enable CSRF protection by the approuter. This is done by setting the CEP.EnableCsrfProtection property to true for all dynamic destinations where their respective backend doesn’t handle CSRF protection.  If your backend is already protected, there’s no need to add this property. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-18\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3119 ---\nComponent: SAP Java Buildpack\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 1.93.0\nDescription: SAP Java Buildpack 1 has been updated from version 1.92.0 to 1.93.0. Updated components:      Apache Tomcat 9 is updated from version 9.0.86 to 9.0.87      Apache TomEE 7 is updated from version 7.0.9.sap-41 to 7.0.9.sap-42      PostgreSQL JDBC Driver (postgresql.version) is updated from 42.7.2 to 42.7.3      SAP HANA Driver (hana.driver.2.X.X) is updated from version 2.19.16 to 2.20.11    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-08\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3120 ---\nComponent: SAP Java Buildpack\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 2.6.0\nDescription: SAP Java Buildpack 2 has been updated from version 2.4.0 to 2.5.0. Updated components:      Apache Tomcat 10 is updated from version 10.1.19 to 10.1.20      PostgreSQL JDBC Driver (postgresql.version) is updated from 42.7.2 to 42.7.3      SAP HANA Driver (hana.driver.2.X.X) is updated from 